      "id": "msg_mockS03",
      "sessionId": "ses_mockHostSugar",
      "seq": 3,
      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedAmara"
      },
      "content": "Taxes change prices, and prices change behaviour — that's the whole mechanism, and it works best on cheap, habitual, heavily marketed products. Sugary drinks are exactly that, and the cost lands hardest on the kids and lower-income families who drink the most of them, while the revenue can fund the very things that make the healthy choice easier. Victor will call this paternalism; I'd call it a nudge that finally makes the price honest about the diabetes and heart disease we all pay for downstream.",
