        "iteration": 1,
        "side": "prop"
      },
      "id": "msg_mockS07",
      "sessionId": "ses_mockHostSugar",
      "seq": 7,
      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedAmara"
      },
      "content": "Victor says silence isn't consent, but nobody consents to paying for someone else's heart attack either — that's the cost we're already subsidising. On regressivity: yes, a flat tax bites harder on small budgets, and that's a fair hit, not a knockout. But the same families pay the steepest price for the diseases these drinks drive, so designing the tax to fund cheap, accessible alternatives answers the objection rather than dodging it. His liberty point rests on a false picture — autonomy in a market where the price has been kept artificially low. That's the open question the house must decide: honest pricing, or a subsidy we don't name.",
      "status": "complete",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-22T13:20:15.874Z",
      "emotion": "thinking",
      "emotionSource": "classifier",
